/// known-gap: interp checks erase conditions only at the end of the tick
/// An erase condition that calls the program's own code (a method, an
/// action, `:invoke`) may roll dice inside it, so like `pick` it is checked
/// once a tick, at the end, however many actions change the object.
<>Mote |
    ~age: 0
    every 1 tick
        self >> age |= self >> age + 1
    end
    every 1 tick
        self >> age |= self >> age + 1
    end
    act risky()
        say("checked")
        return (pick 1 from 1...1000000) == 0
    end
    transition erase when (self.risky())
    end
xx
:rand_seed(1)
m <> Mote | age: 0
tick()
say(m >> age)
